---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, pageSchema } from '../../lib/schema';

const crumbs = [{ label: 'About Evergreen Counseling Collective' }];
---

<Layout
 title="About Evergreen Counseling Collective | Fort Collins, Colorado"
 description="Learn about Evergreen Counseling Collective, a private counseling practice for adults in Fort Collins, Colorado."
 schema={pageSchema([breadcrumbSchema(crumbs, Astro.url.pathname)])}
>
 <PageHero
 eyebrow="About Evergreen"
 title="A small counseling practice with a slower, more personal pace."
 intro="Evergreen Counseling Collective is Maya Bennett’s Fort Collins practice for adults who want thoughtful individual therapy in a calm, grounded setting."
 crumbs={crumbs}
 />

 <section class="section">
 <div class="container grid grid--2">
 <div>
 <p class="eyebrow">The Evergreen idea</p>
 <h2>Make enough room to hear yourself think.</h2>
 </div>

 <div>
 <p>
 Evergreen is built around a simple idea: therapy does not need to rush to be
 useful. Sometimes the most productive place to begin is by slowing down long
 enough to notice what has been happening and what keeps asking for attention.
 </p>

 <p>
 Sessions can stay focused while still leaving space for uncertainty, context,
 and the parts of a story that do not fit neatly into a checklist.
 </p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>

 <section class="section section--tint">
 <div class="container grid grid--3">
 <article class="card">
 <h3>A steady pace</h3>
 <p>
 The work can move thoughtfully rather than urgently, with time to understand
 what matters before deciding what to do with it.
 </p>
 </article>

 <article class="card">
 <h3>Conversation with room in it</h3>
 <p>
 Questions, pauses, uncertainty, and changing your mind can all belong in the
 process. Therapy does not have to sound polished to be meaningful.
 </p>
 </article>

 <article class="card">
 <h3>Attention to context</h3>
 <p>
 Work, relationships, health, identity, responsibilities, and the environment
 around you can all shape how an experience feels and what support makes sense.
 </p>
 </article>
 </div>
 </section>

 <section class="section">
 <div class="container grid grid--2">
 <div>
 <p class="eyebrow">Finding your starting point</p>
 <h2>You can begin with a feeling, a pattern, or a question.</h2>
 </div>

 <div>
 <p>
 The Services page offers a practical overview of concerns Maya commonly works
 with. It is there to help you orient yourself, not to make you choose the one
 perfect category before contacting the practice.
 </p>

 <p>
 Maya’s profile gives a closer look at the tone of her work and the approaches
 she may draw from when they fit what is happening in the room.
 </p>

 <div class="about-links">
 <a class="link-arrow" href="/services/">
 See areas of support
 </a>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>

 <section class="section section--tint">
 <div class="container grid grid--2">
 <div>
 <p class="eyebrow">The person behind Evergreen</p>
 <h2>Meet Maya Bennett, LPC.</h2>
 </div>

 <div>
 <p>
 Maya brings a calm, curious presence to individual counseling and values work
 that feels both grounded and genuinely useful to the person sitting across
 from her.
 </p>

 <a class="link-arrow" href="/about/maya-bennett/">
 Read Maya’s profile
 </a>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>
</Layout>

<style>
 .about-links{
 display:grid;
 gap:.5rem;
 margin-top:1.25rem
 }
</style>
